// M5-A3P-1014. Ch21 H07 "Sefir, phase 3: the Letting" (P, 5 min). act3_ending.md §2 H07; README
// rule 3. Asha steps off the battle timeline and SINGS THE EIGHTH VERSE, the first and only time words and tune meet.
// Her verse is a countdown entry the party protects (Combat). Her voice is the music (`the_letting`, diegetic, an
// ORIGINAL melody: the first verse's phrase turned upward; the voice decision is SPEC §16 Q4/Q5). The palette rotates
// from cool held to warm released; the sleeve unravels from the cuff upward over the last 6 s (art asha.md S8), into
// RISING motes (§0 rule 5). THE VERSE IS AUDIO'S VERSE 8 (docs/kb/audio/lamptongue.md §2, §3), sung whole, the only
// time in the game; it ends on "tash" (let go), where every other verse ends on "mir". Until SPEC §16 Q4/Q5 chooses a
// voice the vocalise carries these vowels; the lines show as sung captions (#sung).
title: ch21_the_letting
location: ch21/heart
---
@camera HT13
@anim asha step_forward
@music the_letting fade=0.0
<<event start_battle ch21_sefir_letting>>
===
title: ch21_the_letting_verse
---
// Played by Combat as the countdown runs: one line per quarter of it.
Asha [determined]: Ish oan, ish oan, #line:ch21_letting_001 #sung #lamptongue #notr #tn:"Lamptongue, the Eighth Verse (lamptongue.md verse 8): keep exactly as written. Sung."
Asha [tender]: vey hal, ennu tash, #line:ch21_letting_002 #sung #lamptongue #notr #tn:"Lamptongue: keep exactly as written."
Asha [tender]: oan re, oan re... #line:ch21_letting_003 #sung #lamptongue #notr #tn:"Lamptongue: keep exactly as written."
Asha [tender]: ...tash. #line:ch21_letting_004 #sung #lamptongue #notr #tn:"Lamptongue: keep exactly as written. The last word of the game's song: 'let go'."
===
title: ch21_the_letting_sleeve
---
// Played by Combat over the countdown's last 6 s.
@vfx glimmer_lift at=asha_sleeve count=7 motion=spiral_up rate=slow
@wait 6.0
===
